# Database & Deployment Documentation — db/

This document describes the contents of the `db/` folder, explains the database design, and provides instructions for setup and deployment.

## 1. Folder Contents

```text
db/
├── README.md                    ← this file
├── erd.md                       ← ERD (Mermaid source)
├── erd.dbml                     ← ERD (DBML source)
├── erd.png                      ← ERD image
├── schema.sql                   ← database schema
├── seed_data.sql                ← sample and test data
├── init_db.py                   ← initializes the database
├── progress_tracker.py          ← manages batch job progress
├── resources/
│   ├── conflict_policy.md
│   ├── case_type_policy.md
│   └── assignment_policy.md
└── prompts/
    ├── conflict_check_prompt.md
    ├── case_review_prompt.md
    └── lawyer_assignment_prompt.md
```

## 2. How to Run

```bash
cd db
python3 init_db.py
```

This script:

* Deletes any existing `case_intake.db`.
* Creates all tables from `schema.sql`.
* Loads the sample data from `seed_data.sql`.
* Prints the row count for each table.

The project uses SQLite, so no database server or additional configuration is required.

---

## 3. Why SQLite

SQLite was chosen because it is lightweight, requires no server setup, and makes the project easy to run and reproduce. It supports foreign keys, CHECK constraints, and indexes, which are sufficient for this project. The schema is also portable and can be migrated to databases such as PostgreSQL or SQL Server with only minor type changes.

---

## 4. SQLite Type Mapping

| ERD Type | SQLite Storage | Enforcement                  |
| -------- | -------------- | ---------------------------- |
| UUID     | `TEXT`         | Generated by the application |
| ENUM     | `TEXT`         | `CHECK` constraint           |
| JSON     | `TEXT`         | Parsed in application code   |
| BOOLEAN  | `INTEGER`      | `CHECK (0,1)`                |
| DATETIME | `TEXT`         | ISO-8601 format              |

---

## 5. Notable Schema Decisions

* The `case` table references `case_type_policy` instead of storing case types directly, keeping policy rules in a single source of truth.
* The table name `"case"` is quoted because `CASE` is a reserved SQL keyword.
* `audit_log.entity_id` is not a foreign key because it may reference different entity types.
* `conflict_check.batch_job_id` is nullable to support both individual and batch conflict checks.

---

## 6. Seed Data

The seed data includes both normal and edge-case scenarios to demonstrate:

* Authorization checks
* Conflict detection
* Lawyer assignment validation
* Batch progress tracking
* Audit logging

---

## 7. Resources & Prompts

The `resources/` and `prompts/` folders contain static reference documents used by the MCP server. Resources provide policy information, while prompts provide reusable templates for common tasks. Keeping each document in a separate file makes registration and maintenance straightforward.

---

## 8. Progress Tracking

`progress_tracker.py` manages the lifecycle of long-running batch jobs by creating jobs, updating progress, and marking them as completed or failed. The MCP server uses these updates to send progress notifications during execution.
